 ## Why this does not settle the intended research question
 
-[FS], Problem 1.1, asks for some positive beta_0 with a conclusion for small beta in m=n^(2-beta). Its Theorem 1.2 proves the H2 bound, with a stronger adjacent-edge condition, for fixed 0<beta<1/5 and sufficiently large n. Our obstruction has delta=2^(-6/5)n^(-4/5), outside that range. The paper's concluding remarks retain the internal strong-C6 density-power question. We do not infer a solution to it from the malformed unrestricted version.
